(1003619, 119985, 3080, '<td valign="top">What''s up with the 2 sided border?  If it was an accident, it''s pretty sloppy presentation, if it was on purpose, I think it''s aweful.  Lighting seems to be very dull.  I think that with a little more lighting, not only would it tone down the distraction shadows, but it could bring out some more detail.  I think this fits the challenge nicely, and the subject is neat, just needs something else to make it really punch.  A little extra light could definatley help that on it''s way.  ~Heather~</td>', 'What''s up with the 2 sided border?  If it was an accident, it''s pretty sloppy presentation, if it was on purpose, I think it''s aweful.  Lighting seems to be very dull.  I think that with a little more lighting, not only would it tone down the distraction shadows, but it could bring out some more detail.  I think this fits the challenge nicely, and the subject is neat, just needs something else to make it really punch.  A little extra light could definatley help that on it''s way.  ~Heather~', '2004-11-10 11:41:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1003621, 119702, 3080, '<td valign="top">True, but maybe not close enough for THIS challenge.  It''s a good photo, I definatley give it that, but I don''t consider 1/2 a large cat to be extreme close up.  I realize that you couldn''t get any closer, but then maybe you could have gotten a different subject.  It looks like you got a great pic of a cat and decided to enter it anyway even though it''s not extreme close up.  Lighting is great, and focus and calrity are great, beautiful cat, and background is not distracting.   Like I said, great photo, but maybe not for this challenge.  ~Heather~</td>', 'True, but maybe not close enough for THIS challenge.  It''s a good photo, I definatley give it that, but I don''t consider 1/2 a large cat to be extreme close up.  I realize that you couldn''t get any closer, but then maybe you could have gotten a different subject.  It looks like you got a great pic of a cat and decided to enter it anyway even though it''s not extreme close up.  Lighting is great, and focus and calrity are great, beautiful cat, and background is not distracting.   Like I said, great photo, but maybe not for this challenge.  ~Heather~', '2004-11-10 11:44:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1003623, 118286, 19010, '<td valign="top">Normaly I woulddnt have liked this shot at all the lack of focus in the background is almost dizzying. But in this case of stage fright. I feel it is almost the most important aspect. I can feel the dizzyness a person with stage fright would have at a microphone.. Great job 7</td>', 'Normaly I woulddnt have liked this shot at all the lack of focus in the background is almost dizzying. But in this case of stage fright. I feel it is almost the most important aspect. I can feel the dizzyness a person with stage fright would have at a microphone.. Great job 7', '2004-11-10 11:44:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1003624, 119057, 3080, '<td valign="top">This shot came up ''randomly'' on every single page of thumbnails for me, so I''d better comment on it.  I love it.  Simple, extremely close up, great focus/clarity.  And where you chose to place the subject within the frame is good as well.  Maybe not the most ''beautiful'' or ''stunning'' of pics, but well done, and appropriate for this challenge. ~Heather~</td>', 'This shot came up ''randomly'' on every single page of thumbnails for me, so I''d better comment on it.  I love it.  Simple, extremely close up, great focus/clarity.  And where you chose to place the subject within the frame is good as well.  Maybe not the most ''beautiful'' or ''stunning'' of pics, but well done, and appropriate for this challenge. ~Heather~', '2004-11-10 11:46:12.000000', NULL, 1),
