(1010221, 120021, 19333, '<td valign="top">Well, maybe I woldn''t call it a macro. What about a take focused the other way around? I mean focus on the wire in front an let the background OOF. Nice and inspiring pic anyway. Maybe you can send it to Amnesty International.<br/> <br/><i>edited for spelling</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-17 11:23:22.</i></td>', 'Well, maybe I woldn''t call it a macro. What about a take focused the other way around? I mean focus on the wire in front an let the background OOF. Nice and inspiring pic anyway. Maybe you can send it to Amnesty International. edited for spelling', '2004-11-14 05:50:34.000000', '2004-11-17 11:23:22.000000', 1),
(1010233, 120274, 8367, '<td valign="top">I love this concept but feel the highlights or blown areas hurt this photo. The subject choice is great and it would be worth experimenting more with the lighting. IMH experience, I''ve found studio lighting to be most difficult.</td>', 'I love this concept but feel the highlights or blown areas hurt this photo. The subject choice is great and it would be worth experimenting more with the lighting. IMH experience, I''ve found studio lighting to be most difficult.', '2004-11-14 07:16:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1010244, 120114, 21124, '<td valign="top">I am sorry but I do not like this unusual effect. The composition is interesting, but some more natural colors would perhaps have been better.</td>', 'I am sorry but I do not like this unusual effect. The composition is interesting, but some more natural colors would perhaps have been better.', '2004-11-14 07:56:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1010245, 118264, 21124, '<td valign="top">I like to colors a lot.<br/>In my opinion, the light is still a bit "harsh". It looks like a direct flash. Perhaps bouncing the flash would have improved it.<br/>I would also have preffered more sharpness on the paper clips. It seems that your camera is focused on the separation between the compartiments rather than beeing focused on the clips.<br/>6</td>', 'I like to colors a lot.In my opinion, the light is still a bit "harsh". It looks like a direct flash. Perhaps bouncing the flash would have improved it.I would also have preffered more sharpness on the paper clips. It seems that your camera is focused on the separation between the compartiments rather than beeing focused on the clips.6', '2004-11-14 07:59:48.000000', NULL, 1),
