(1014944, 120091, 23394, '<td valign="top">no clue why this finished here...only two things that i can think of would be 1) to have shot it on an angle, and 2) to have had richer colors in the background.  i loved the shot.</td>', 'no clue why this finished here...only two things that i can think of would be 1) to have shot it on an angle, and 2) to have had richer colors in the background.  i loved the shot.', '2004-11-17 00:51:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1014948, 120153, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bledford:</b></div><hr/><i> Great shot.  I''m curious about your indication of the use NeatImage <b>twice</b> on the image.  Anyway, great shot and congrats on the ribbon.  You are now the official "guy who keeps winning ribbons" guy. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks Brad,<br/>Here is the original shot, resized only. (compressed to save portfolio space)<br/>One run through NI was for obvious noise issues with the E-10 at ISO160.<br/>After basics, I ran it again just to see what would happen, and found it gave the opaque look to the rings on the bottle neck.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=122216" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/122216.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/122216.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/19708/thumb/122216.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-17 00:57:35.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by bledford: Great shot.  I''m curious about your indication of the use NeatImage twice on the image.  Anyway, great shot and congrats on the ribbon.  You are now the official "guy who keeps winning ribbons" guy.  Thanks Brad,Here is the original shot, resized only. (compressed to save portfolio space)One run through NI was for obvious noise issues with the E-10 at ISO160.After basics, I ran it again just to see what would happen, and found it gave the opaque look to the rings on the bottle neck.', '2004-11-17 00:53:07.000000', '2004-11-17 00:57:35.000000', 0),
(1014953, 119706, 19408, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments!</td>', 'thanks for the comments!', '2004-11-17 00:55:12.000000', NULL, 0),
