(1018820, 118354, 19260, '<td valign="top">thanks for all the comments it has been helpful. Yes it seems out of focus because of the moist in the glass. I used cold soda for the liquid. :)</td>', 'thanks for all the comments it has been helpful. Yes it seems out of focus because of the moist in the glass. I used cold soda for the liquid. :)', '2004-11-18 00:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1018824, 119891, 24495, '<td valign="top">I dont agree to the brutal remarks given by most. The subject is good, and so is the composition. The glare seems to be due to the glazed ceramic surface. The only doubt is whether it is out of focus, or inadequate depth of field due to extreme close up! (Well, for who donot know, this is the transistors/resisters used in electronic equipment, and even transisters. The length may be just less than half inch!).</td>', 'I dont agree to the brutal remarks given by most. The subject is good, and so is the composition. The glare seems to be due to the glazed ceramic surface. The only doubt is whether it is out of focus, or inadequate depth of field due to extreme close up! (Well, for who donot know, this is the transistors/resisters used in electronic equipment, and even transisters. The length may be just less than half inch!).', '2004-11-18 00:20:45.000000', NULL, 0),
