(1028299, 118625, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>Hello, other than the handle this is a good sharp picture. Like Konador has already stated is that this photo would probably benefit from being a B&amp;W image due to it''s lack of color. I think that and using an aperture of about 16 or higher would give your shot sharpness all over. I like that you thought out of the box in choosing your subject. This is definitely something that is different and that with a few adjustments would look much better. <br/></td>', '::Critique Club:: Hello, other than the handle this is a good sharp picture. Like Konador has already stated is that this photo would probably benefit from being a B&W image due to it''s lack of color. I think that and using an aperture of about 16 or higher would give your shot sharpness all over. I like that you thought out of the box in choosing your subject. This is definitely something that is different and that with a few adjustments would look much better. ', '2004-11-23 02:12:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1028313, 120105, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>First off I like whats going on here. I agree with Konador stating that this could have used a bit more contrast. I do think that a smaller aperture would have been better also, now as to how much. I don''t know if you want to see all the way down due to the background might not be as appealing as you would want it, I don''t know because I can''t make it out. I think the zipper itself should be more in the frame, maybe not center but just not hanging off like that. I like your subject and your attempt. <br/></td>', '::Critique Club:: First off I like whats going on here. I agree with Konador stating that this could have used a bit more contrast. I do think that a smaller aperture would have been better also, now as to how much. I don''t know if you want to see all the way down due to the background might not be as appealing as you would want it, I don''t know because I can''t make it out. I think the zipper itself should be more in the frame, maybe not center but just not hanging off like that. I like your subject and your attempt. ', '2004-11-23 02:20:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1028325, 119734, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>I really like your subject. I think a few things that could help this photo would be smaller aperture making the whole thing sharp. Another would be a different table top to place it on, maybe blackI dont know. I do love the other colors, and its eyes. Great! One more small thing, its eyes seem a bit hazy due to the light, but other than a diffuser or something along those lines I dont know how to fix that. I think the border works also.  Once again, great subject and attempt.</td>', '::Critique Club:: I really like your subject. I think a few things that could help this photo would be smaller aperture making the whole thing sharp. Another would be a different table top to place it on, maybe blackI dont know. I do love the other colors, and its eyes. Great! One more small thing, its eyes seem a bit hazy due to the light, but other than a diffuser or something along those lines I dont know how to fix that. I think the border works also.  Once again, great subject and attempt.', '2004-11-23 02:27:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1028450, 118629, 25843, '<td valign="top">very nice :-)</td>', 'very nice :-)', '2004-11-23 06:02:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1028594, 119862, 19010, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :) <br/> <br/>GENERAL: I think this is almost an ''abstract'' image. I takes a person a while to realize what they are looking at. I''m not familiar with the animal that the name buster refers too. I was however after looking at the picture for a good while able to guess that it was a cat.<br/> <br/>FOCUS: I think the DoF in this image may be to short. Only a very small section on the front of the paw seems to be in focus. The portion of the paw that is in focus however is very crisp and has a lot of wonderfull detail. <br/> <br/>BACKGROUND: I think another improvement on this shot would be in the use of smoother background. I like the denim like material, and feel you chose and captured it well, however I think that the long dark wrinkles draw you away from the paw. Perhaps if it was laid smooth it would help instead of distract.<br/> <br/>LIGHTING: I personally would Like to have seen this lit from the other side. I feel a soft light from the right pointing towards the bottom of the paw would have given this a softer feel. As is the highlights are overwhelming and burn out all of the great colors. It also would have allowed the viewer to see more of the details on the bottom of the paw.<br/> <br/>OVERALL: This is a shot with alot of possibility. With diferent lighting, and a better DoF I feel this could have easily made another couple of full points in the challenge.I am not a cat fan myself, but I found the details you were trying to show in this photo to very interesting. This could have been a good candidate for a feline heath magazine.  While I''m not overly awed by this shot, I do feel it has potential. I''t is very creative and looks at thinks in a POV that most have never considered. <br/> <br/>Keep up the interesting work<br/> <br/>Tristalisk<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :)  GENERAL: I think this is almost an ''abstract'' image. I takes a person a while to realize what they are looking at. I''m not familiar with the animal that the name buster refers too. I was however after looking at the picture for a good while able to guess that it was a cat. FOCUS: I think the DoF in this image may be to short. Only a very small section on the front of the paw seems to be in focus. The portion of the paw that is in focus however is very crisp and has a lot of wonderfull detail.  BACKGROUND: I think another improvement on this shot would be in the use of smoother background. I like the denim like material, and feel you chose and captured it well, however I think that the long dark wrinkles draw you away from the paw. Perhaps if it was laid smooth it would help instead of distract. LIGHTING: I personally would Like to have seen this lit from the other side. I feel a soft light from the right pointing towards the bottom of the paw would have given this a softer feel. As is the highlights are overwhelming and burn out all of the great colors. It also would have allowed the viewer to see more of the details on the bottom of the paw. OVERALL: This is a shot with alot of possibility. With diferent lighting, and a better DoF I feel this could have easily made another couple of full points in the challenge.I am not a cat fan myself, but I found the details you were trying to show in this photo to very interesting. This could have been a good candidate for a feline heath magazine.  While I''m not overly awed by this shot, I do feel it has potential. I''t is very creative and looks at thinks in a POV that most have never considered.  Keep up the interesting work Tristalisk ', '2004-11-23 09:17:58.000000', NULL, 0),
