(1029267, 118656, 656, '<td valign="top">Another shot with great initial impact. The colours and patterns are really strong and the leading lines give a lot of visual interest.  Only issues I have are the high contrast, out of focus areas in the upper left and lower right, that draw my eyes.  The yellow line leads off to the background, walking me through the image, but I get lost in the rear ''V'' shape without really anywhere to go.  This is a subject with a lot of potential.  <br/> <br/>The soft foreground and background, with only the midground in sharp focus confuses my eye a little too - I start in the out of focus region, move through the sharpness and back to out of focus again - I think I''d prefer it if it was sharp at one end or the other and lead off to either sharpness or an out of focus area.  This would probably require manual focus setting on your camera, rather than using one of the AF points.  You could focus and recompose but that often isn''t the best way to achieve something like that.   For this - I''d probably try and have the very tip of the yellow line in sharpest focus.<br/> <br/>Also worth checking the edges again - particularly for the lighter red/ orange regions creeping in at the bottom - They could probably have been cropped out in this case.</td>', 'Another shot with great initial impact. The colours and patterns are really strong and the leading lines give a lot of visual interest.  Only issues I have are the high contrast, out of focus areas in the upper left and lower right, that draw my eyes.  The yellow line leads off to the background, walking me through the image, but I get lost in the rear ''V'' shape without really anywhere to go.  This is a subject with a lot of potential.   The soft foreground and background, with only the midground in sharp focus confuses my eye a little too - I start in the out of focus region, move through the sharpness and back to out of focus again - I think I''d prefer it if it was sharp at one end or the other and lead off to either sharpness or an out of focus area.  This would probably require manual focus setting on your camera, rather than using one of the AF points.  You could focus and recompose but that often isn''t the best way to achieve something like that.   For this - I''d probably try and have the very tip of the yellow line in sharpest focus. Also worth checking the edges again - particularly for the lighter red/ orange regions creeping in at the bottom - They could probably have been cropped out in this case.', '2004-11-23 17:09:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1029283, 119900, 22843, '<td valign="top">I always thought the blue lights from my cell phone were real cool, thats what I wanted to emphisize im my pic, I should have just shot them and left the screen out. I took this pic one night when I was messing with my camera in the dark using slow shutter speeds.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-23 17:28:03.</i></td>', 'I always thought the blue lights from my cell phone were real cool, thats what I wanted to emphisize im my pic, I should have just shot them and left the screen out. I took this pic one night when I was messing with my camera in the dark using slow shutter speeds.', '2004-11-23 17:26:31.000000', '2004-11-23 17:28:03.000000', 0),
(1029352, 119737, 23913, '<td valign="top">(i''m just going back over results) One can tell that this is a leaf but it is well shot and the grays are very vivid (if that is a good way to describe [the tone]).<br/> <br/>anyway congrats on comming in 326 out of 528 this challenge was a big 1. (so much so that i have just now gone through and seen all the images in there full res.[size]).</td>', '(i''m just going back over results) One can tell that this is a leaf but it is well shot and the grays are very vivid (if that is a good way to describe [the tone]). anyway congrats on comming in 326 out of 528 this challenge was a big 1. (so much so that i have just now gone through and seen all the images in there full res.[size]).', '2004-11-23 18:50:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1029411, 118524, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>This shot is great, composition, lighting, contrast, and angle. The only thing I can think of is over sharpening in Photoshop, if thats not the case and this is how the person really looks then disregard. I think the chin could have benefited from a slightly smaller aperture to make it pop alittle more. I wish you could have cloned out that noise hair, not that distracting but once I saw it my eye kept going back, but this was a basic challenge so it was against the rules to do such a move. I like the overall image and subject  and think I would have given it a 6.</td>', '::Critique Club:: This shot is great, composition, lighting, contrast, and angle. The only thing I can think of is over sharpening in Photoshop, if thats not the case and this is how the person really looks then disregard. I think the chin could have benefited from a slightly smaller aperture to make it pop alittle more. I wish you could have cloned out that noise hair, not that distracting but once I saw it my eye kept going back, but this was a basic challenge so it was against the rules to do such a move. I like the overall image and subject  and think I would have given it a 6.', '2004-11-23 19:41:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1031326, 120178, 15592, '<td valign="top">this is really amazing!  i have been looking at it now for some time and can''t seem to stop!  i love it.  i don''t know how you get the water droplet to stay on the end of the brush and then do everything else that you have to in order to take the photo!!  very well done and even though i didn''t vote i am pleased to see that it scored so well as i can see that it must have been an extremely difficult set up.  very well done!  you should be very proud of your work as it''s a real "WOW" entry!</td>', 'this is really amazing!  i have been looking at it now for some time and can''t seem to stop!  i love it.  i don''t know how you get the water droplet to stay on the end of the brush and then do everything else that you have to in order to take the photo!!  very well done and even though i didn''t vote i am pleased to see that it scored so well as i can see that it must have been an extremely difficult set up.  very well done!  you should be very proud of your work as it''s a real "WOW" entry!', '2004-11-24 12:20:20.000000', NULL, 0),
